WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.920
<i>I'd never seen a ghost or a yokai,</i>

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>and I didn't really care if they existed.</i>

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.720
<i>I didn't think they were that scary.</i>

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.480
<i>I just wasn't interested in them at all.</i>

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:23.020
<i>Instead, my head was filled 
with real-world problems.</i>

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.980
Senpai, don't forget us.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.760
Promise us!

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.080
I've been waiting, Inaba.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.250
Now, then...

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.480
I've been waiting to pound that 
face of yours flat, Hase.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.030
Same here.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.030
I've been waiting for a chance 
to have a real fight with you.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.150
Don't whine later—

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.560
Ow...

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.820
You were really hitting hard.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.720
My mouth tastes like blood.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.220
This was your idea, right?

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.980
Well, this is to celebrate our 
middle school graduation.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.400
I wanted to try something like this.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.660
Congratulations on making it into JTB, Inaba.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.140
Same to you, Hase.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.250
Top of the class, at a famous 
school. Impressive.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.930
You really are amazing, Hase.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.310
Now, you're as good as admitted into Tokyo U.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.720
It's your first step toward being 
a super-elite businessman!

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.930
You're just as amazing...

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.640
Wasn't going to a residential 
high school your dream?

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.060
Yeah!

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.130
I'm gonna do my best.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.090
I'll learn a lot and get certifications.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.980
And after graduation, I'll be able 
to start work as a businessman!

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.570
Hey, Inaba...

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.470
Are you really okay?

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.410
Yeah!

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.490
<i>This spring,</i>

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:26.490
<i>I, Yushi Inaba, was accepted into 
Joutou Business High School.</i>

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.170
<i>For so long, I've wanted to 
live in a dorm, on my own,</i>

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.320
<i>and this is my chance.</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.950
<i>Now, I can finally leave my uncle's house.</i>

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.850
<i>That's right.</i>

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.280
<i>Now, I can live on my own.</i>

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:50.230
<b>Update JTB Dorm Burns Down 
Cause Under Investigation</b>

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.140
<i>This afternoon,</i>

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.870
<i>the Joutou Business High School 
dorm was the scene of a fire.</i>

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.940
<i>The building burned to the ground.</i>

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.720
Seriously?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:31.370
<b>First Haunting 
Yushi and Kotobuki-so</b>

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.720
Looking for a room at this time of year?

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.330
What's your budget?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.300
20,000 or 30,000? I don't even 
know what to do with that.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.820
There's this thing called a market that says

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.050
the cheapest rate here is 50,000.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.250
We're closed now.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.430
And you can't get a room without a guarantor.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.930
No parents?

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.160
You're a minor, aren't you?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.610
Then, why not just stay with your uncle?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.940
I mean, not much else to be done.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.620
Not much else to be done, huh?

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.070
We got a message

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:18.630
that the dorm reconstruction 
will take about six months.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.190
Oh, dear...

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.540
But I'm glad you weren't there.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.410
B-But I...

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.900
My move...

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.300
Then, what will you do?

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.960
What? Well, I mean...

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.970
He'll have to stay here while 
he goes to school!

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.650
Yeah, I guess he will.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.740
E-Eriko...

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.390
I-I'll take care of this, somehow!

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.140
<i>What the hell is "somehow," though?</i>

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:04.930
<i>In the end, I'm just a
completely helpless kid,</i>

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.650
<i>whose life is dictated by others,</i>

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.350
<i>and I can't do anything.</i>

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.880
Are you really okay?

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.030
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.700
Mister...

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.200
You're looking for a room?

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.480
Try over there.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.290
<b>Land Apartments Offices 
Maeda Realty, Inc.</b>

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.300
I'm sure you'll find a good one.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.790
Maeda... Realty?

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.140
<b>Land Apartments Offices 
Maeda Realty, Inc.</b>

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.680
U-Um...

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.480
Welcome.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.900
<b>Land Apartments Offices 
Maeda Realty, Inc.</b>

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:07.450
A JTB student, huh?

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.570
Sorry to hear about what happened.

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:11.230
Yeah.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.900
I've got a one that's a ten-minute walk 
to Takanodai Higashi Station.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.680
A 15-square-meter Japanese-style 
room and 3-meter closet.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.990
Southern exposure.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:24.420
The toilet and bath are shared, 
but it comes with food.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.840
Oh, and also utilities.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.000
And the rent is only 25,000 yen!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.010
<b>Kotobuki-so     25,000 Yen</b>

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.170
Seriously?!

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:33.840
Yeah. Seriously.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.840
<b>Kotobuki-so     25,000 Yen</b>

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:39.850
Is there anything I should 
know about this place...

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.180
There are ghosts...

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:44.600
Huh?

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:49.490
Actually, I have a room in 
that apartment building.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.840
I use it as storage...

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.080
Why not rent it?

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:55.520
Can I?!

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:59.190
You only need to stay six months, 
until they rebuild the dorm, right?

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.570
Th-Thank you!

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.090
The building's name is "Kotobuki-so."

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.810
How do you like it?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.960
Pretty classy, right?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.730
Y-Yeah...

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.190
<i>The Kotobuki-so, huh?</i>

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.150
<i>I wonder how old it is.</i>

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:54.710
Here, you go.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.320
This is the key for room 202.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.080
From now on, that's your room.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.020
<i>My own room!</i>

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:09.510
If you like, use the furniture.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:12.060
And you don't mind books on 
the bookshelves, do you?

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.090
No, not at all!

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.890
Reimei Isshiki!

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.610
I'm a big fan!

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.400
You read Isshiki-san, too?

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.030
You're a bit old-fashioned.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.090
Yeah.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.980
I borrowed one from a friend 
named Hase and loved it!

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.130
They may seem grotesque, 
but they're actually really refined.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.540
I especially like the gap between 
them and the author's photo...

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.050
I wondered what that noise was. Are you new?

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:41.880
Reimei Isshiki!

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.720
Isshiki-sensei!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:44.860
Is it really you?

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.310
It really is.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:50.220
Isshiki-sensei, you live here?

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.460
Yeah, for over a decade...

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.140
But I'm considered one of 
the newer residents.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.570
I-Is that so?

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.890
<i>I can live in the same building 
as one of my favorite authors.</i>

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.170
<i>This is amazing!</i>

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.990
Isshiki-san, is there someone new?

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:10.500
Yep.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.170
I'm Akine Kuga!

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.550
Nice to meet you.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.580
Akine-san?

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.730
Akine Kuga-chan, from room 204.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.940
A second-year at Takanodai High.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.930
She lives on her own, just like you.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.820
On her own? Even though she's a girl?

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.490
Isn't she lonely?

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.350
Not at all...

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.900
Living here is so much fun.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.810
I hope you enjoy it, too!

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:38.960
All right!

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:41.130
I'll help you start unpacking.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.990
Is this all you have? There isn't much here.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.240
Oh, you don't have to...

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.070
You kids have fun.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.440
Okay, thank you!

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:54.960
I see.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.090
Your parents passed away, huh?

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.800
Yeah, when I was in seventh grade, 
they died in a car accident.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.890
My parents died suddenly, and I was alone.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.240
My uncle's family took me in.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.290
But my family was an average 
salaryman's household,

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:17.290
so we didn't have any money.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.460
I'm sure I put a lot of financial 
pressure on my uncle's family.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.120
And my cousin, who's a year older,

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.140
Eriko, was harsher than I'd expected.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.860
I couldn't let them support me forever.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:37.450
So I decided on a school with a dorm.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.840
But the dorm burned down in a fire,

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.520
and now I'm here.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.920
I see.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.750
But I'm just fine!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.890
That was three years ago.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.390
Now, I need to do my best on my own.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.780
A-Akine-san?

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.370
You needn't be in such a hurry to grow up.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.110
R-Right.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:09.180
All right! Let's unpack the rest 
of your stuff, Yushi-kun.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.030
Okay!

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.860
That's most of it, huh?

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.450
Thank you.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.470
I wanted to introduce you 
to the other residents,

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.130
but they're all out.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:23.170
Well, they'll be back, eventually.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.580
Oh?

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.140
Don't worry!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.290
They're all really nice!

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.720
Indeed.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.230
Akine-chan might be the scariest one here.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.200
Jeez, Isshiki-san, I'll get mad!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.150
<i>I'm not that worried.</i>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.500
I was kidding.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.390
<i>Looking at these two,</i>

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.480
Want one?

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.860
<i>I can tell exactly the kind of place this is.</i>

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.560
Yes! Thank you!

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.690
<i>I'm glad I came here.</i>

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.330
Yushi-kun, dinner's ready. Let's go.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.710
Okay!

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.370
Oh, yeah. I get food, too.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.550
I wonder how it is.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.470
This way, Yushi-kun.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.290
Coming!

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.140
Wow!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.660
They said today is your welcome dinner.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.520
I love Ruriko-san!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.370
Let's eat!

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.110
It's good!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.480
Isn't it?

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:31.080
Ruriko-san, the chef, is a genius!

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.160
She always cooks us warm meals.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.510
Ruriko-san?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.030
<i>She cooks in the dark?</i>

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:42.850
<i>Is that really okay?</i>

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.060
Oh, my... Everyone came to eat.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.360
I bet the smell brought them down.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.330
Thanks for the meal!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.030
I'm so full!

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:36.550
That was great, right?

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.030
Y-Yeah.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.930
U-Um, Akine-san...

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.730
The people in the cafeteria...

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.990
Do they all live here?

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.090
Most are neighbors.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:56.040
This place is kind of a local hangout.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.510
A hangout? Is that—

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.450
Look at the time!

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.120
Yushi-kun, I'm heading off.

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.950
Where are you going?

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.610
I've got work.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.050
The night shift at the hospital.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.010
At this hour?

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.630
You go and relax! Bye!

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:18.980
Relax?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.950
I don't know about that.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.010
There are ghosts...

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.840
No way.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.360
They're playing Mahjong.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.970
I know... I'll ask them about 
these apartments.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.590
Um...

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.020
Yushi-kun!

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.920
What's wrong? Why so surprised?

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.840
I-Isshiki-san!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.650
Let's go to the bath.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:25.210
The bath in the basement is amazing!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.180
B-Bath?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.460
This is paradise...

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:40.820
<i>This is the building's basement, isn't it?</i>

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.540
I-Isshiki-san, I've been wondering something.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:49.120
Isn't there something kind of weird...

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.230
about this apartment building?

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.760
There sure is!

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.400
This is a yokai apartment building.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:57.830
A yokai...

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.110
Right, landlord?

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:29.080
Inaba... Hey, Inaba!

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.060
Wake up!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.210
A dream?

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.520
Er... I had this weird dream.

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:39.600
There was this yokai...

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.280
There aren't any yokai, though.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:42.790
What are you talking about?

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:43.960
You're so dumb.

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:45.670
Yeah.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.720
There's a yokai

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:50.170
right here.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.410
H-Huh?

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:57.050
I guess that was a dream?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.600
That was a weird dream, though...

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:04.670
Morning...

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:05.820
Morning!

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.340
Sleep well, chirp?

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:09.680
Wake up and smell the roses, chirp.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:12.900
But they say kids who sleep, grow big, chirp.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.620
And we grew too much!

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.060
I-Isshiki-san!

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.850
Oh, good morning, Yushi-kun.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.010
You had a rough time yesterday, huh?

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:30.410
I knew it.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.930
This is a yokai apartment building.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.810
It actually is?

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:41.210
If you want to go back home, 
I'll help you pack.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.620
I'm back!

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.160
Oh, welcome back, Akine-chan.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.480
Oh, Yushi-kun...

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.350
How did it go last night?

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:54.020
A-Akine-san... Behind you.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.830
Wh-What is that guy?

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.530
Akine-san, watch out! Run!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:19.040
<i>Don't tell me... She's too scared to move?</i>

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:27.090
Damn it.

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:28.320
Akine-san!

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.200
<i>Kin!</i>

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.070
<b>Kin</b>

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.950
I-It's gone.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.870
Akine-san, was that...

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.090
An evil spirit.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.990
Oh, just an evil spirit...

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:06.040
Wait, an e-evil spirit?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:11.330
At the crossing in front of the station, 
he was staring at me the whole time.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:14.980
I ignored him, but I guess 
he got attached to me.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.010
He probably stalked girls his whole life,

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:20.290
and even in death, he can't stop!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:22.160
So I purified him.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.840
P-Purified him?

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.030
Akine-san, are you...

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:29.890
I didn't tell you?

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:32.310
I'm an exorcist!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:34.210
But I'm still training.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.040
An exorcist, huh?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.630
A person who gets rid of spirits 
that cause trouble.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.200
Many things happen, and many 
different people are here.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.610
Great, isn't it?

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.060
This world isn't so bad.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:51.320
So, Yushi-kun?

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.130
What will you do?

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:58.980
I get hungry when I use my power!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.110
Food, food!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.370
I wonder what's for breakfast...

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:07.290
<i>I'd never seen a ghost or a yokai,</i>

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.990
<i>and I didn't really care if they existed.</i>

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:17.210
<i>But it seems as though</i>

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.190
<i>yokai and humans really 
do live together here.</i>

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:25.130
<i>And the name of the place 
is the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:28.830
<i>I'm Yushi Inaba. It's the spring
of my first year of high school.</i>

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.090
<i>My first step toward independence</i>

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:36.500
<i>seems to have landed me somewhere incredible.</i>

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:11.820
You're kidding me...

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:14.310
A yokai apartment building? Seriously?

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:16.310
There are more surprises in store.

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:20.240
Those who live here aren't exactly ordinary!

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:23.000
They seem scarier than the yokai.

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:26.710
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.800
The Residents of the Yokai Apartments.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.800
<b>Second Haunting 
The Residents of the Yokai Apartments</b>

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.930
Er, since they're residents,
they're human, right?

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:33.930
Who can say?
